{"title":"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are the midpoints of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/377291318df52e4f013ab2bf28ee82454a9e57da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f988caff51f7fc88ad40d1d25022c52ffd8f976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636251674ae38bb58e9b70b6d64717afdcf942a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> moves along a line that is parallel to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, how many of the four quantities listed below change?\n</p><p>(a) the length of the segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(b) the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636251674ae38bb58e9b70b6d64717afdcf942a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>(c) the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636251674ae38bb58e9b70b6d64717afdcf942a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>(d) the area of trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e8fd7cb9d437fa759db050c3da133c22828439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABNM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b66755a2c42a83a93ad849254ee5df3266bb45c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((2,0)--(8,0)--(6,4)--cycle); draw((4,2)--(7,2)); draw((1,4)--(9,4),Arrows); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(2,0),SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(8,0),SE); label(&quot;$M$&quot;,(4,2),W); label(&quot;$N$&quot;,(7,2),E); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,(6,4),N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/6/6b612f2e7d03d9dfcc6823d02741b0620b173593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Examine each quantity to determine if it changes or remains constant.\n</p><p>(a) By the midsegment theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8de86eb0d692db1fb791aabda40fd5a665c78cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN=\\frac{1}{2}AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"101\" height=\"37\" />, so it remains constant.\n</p><p>(b) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> moves far to the left or right, the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636251674ae38bb58e9b70b6d64717afdcf942a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> increases without bound, so it changes.\n</p><p>(c) The height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636251674ae38bb58e9b70b6d64717afdcf942a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> remains constant, as does its base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636251674ae38bb58e9b70b6d64717afdcf942a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> remains constant.\n</p><p>(d) The height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e8fd7cb9d437fa759db050c3da133c22828439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABNM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> remains constant, as do the lengths of its bases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e8fd7cb9d437fa759db050c3da133c22828439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABNM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> remains constant.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c2f45ba306e2fa3a8fbeae63fa939779e2b8a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" /> of these quantities changes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_DDM\">Video Solution by DDM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by DDM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j6l55gUDpgo\">https://youtu.be/j6l55gUDpgo</a>\n</p><p>~piggydude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/yf4eWFAmmd0?si=voNN42OoTcS8Z3sz\">https://youtu.be/yf4eWFAmmd0?si=voNN42OoTcS8Z3sz</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10\" title=\"2000 AMC 10\">2000 AMC 10</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Answer_Key\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"200